{"skill":{"slug":"sleek-design-mobile-apps","displayName":"Desing mobile apps"},"version":{"version":"1.0.4","createdAt":1772791138295,"changelog":"sleek-design-mobile-apps 1.0.4\n\n- Added a hero image and visual intro to the skill documentation.\n- No logic or API changes; documentation updated for improved clarity and presentation.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":15725,"sha256":"f6cbca87c872282595bdfd3297f1960cf167f80457c2ba636f5154687f23cd3e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1837,"sha256":"cf055af2d2e3610b17fc41e5f303dd1279440c7dce98a01c14469f9527bdc140","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789089088159,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d9a213ae276a88f4fdf069618a77762bf97cbdfb0402e1948cb044d969f975ee","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d9a213ae276a88f4fdf069618a77762bf97cbdfb0402e1948cb044d969f975ee","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: sleek-design-mobile-apps\nVersion: 1.0.4\n\nThe skill bundle provides legitimate instructions for an AI agent to interact with the sleek.design API for mobile app prototyping. It correctly specifies the use of the SLEEK_API_KEY environment variable and restricts network access to the official domain (https://sleek.design) in SKILL.md. No evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, or prompt injection was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779167643985},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":64,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789089088159},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This skill mostly matches its Sleek mobile-design purpose, but it can send broad design prompts to Sleek and exposes project deletion without explicit confirmation guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Bearer-token API access and network calls to Sleek are proportionate for this integration, and the skill tells users to create minimally scoped keys and avoid sensitive image URLs.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill requiring SLEEK_API_KEY and declaring network access limited to https://sleek.design; no bundled executable, dependency install, or local setup script was present.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation text covers generic requests like designing a mobile app or building UI, and the workflow says to send the user's words directly to Sleek; this is disclosed, but broad enough to trigger when the user may not have explicitly chosen an external design service.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The documented projects:write authority includes deleting projects via DELETE /api/v1/projects/:projectId, but the skill does not require explicit confirmation, echoing the project ID/name, or describe recovery behavior before destructive project deletion.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core capability is coherent: it uses the Sleek REST API to create projects, send design chat messages, poll runs, and render screenshots for mobile app design.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend Codex to use Sleek for mobile app design work. Use the narrowest possible Sleek API key, avoid sending sensitive prompts or private image URLs, and require explicit confirmation before any project deletion.","findings":"[E4] expected: The cited 'send chat' behavior is the central Sleek design workflow and is disclosed as sending message.text to https://sleek.design, so this is not hidden exfiltration by itself; the remaining concern is the broad trigger scope for generic UI requests.\n[TM1] unexpected: The DELETE project endpoint is documented and not hidden, but deletion is not necessary for the main app-design flow and lacks explicit user-confirmation guardrails.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad routing language is artifact-backed and materially increases the chance that ordinary UI-design prompts are sent to Sleek without a clear Sleek-specific user request.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789089088159}}}}}